    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **274 tests, 0 failures**, including the new `Cp13Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation cap: creating an owner is rejected with **400 Bad Request** once 20 owners already share the new owner's registration date.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I added:\n\n1. **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step reading the built `Owner` via `@Val`, counting existing owners in `OwnerRepository` with the same registration date, and throwing when the count reaches the limit of 20.\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`** \u2014 a checked escalation exception.\n\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the existing handler style.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` right after `defaultRegistrationDate` (so the registration date is populated first) under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe check runs after the default registration date is applied (today), so the 21st owner created today is rejected while owners registered on other dates are unaffected.",
